  "id": "Compound::DB00198 - Gene::4759",
  "verbalization": "Oseltamivir is linked to Neu2 through a series of molecular interactions that suggest a potential role in modulating sialidase activity. The evidence indicates that Oseltamivir binds to Neu1, which is involved in the exo-alpha-sialidase activity, and this activity is also present in Neu2. This suggests that Oseltamivir may influence Neu2 through a shared pathway involving sialidase activity. The connection between Oseltamivir and Neu2 is further supported by the fact that Oseltamivir is classified as an antiviral agent and an organonitrogen compound, which may imply a broader pharmacological profile. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Oseltamivir could interact with Neu2, potentially affecting sialidase activity and contributing to its antiviral effects.",
